OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Members of the NUM have voted not to
OL,6, impose a national levy of 50p to
OL,7, support miners sacked in the pit strike
OL,8,F
OL,9,FA total of 109,150 votes were cast
OL,10,Fin a national ballot, with 46 per cent
OL,11,Fsupporting the levy and 54 per cent
OL,12,Fagainst it.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FAreas covering a total of nearly
OL,15,F77,000 miners chose not to vote
OL,16,Fin their union's first national ballot
OL,17,Ffor four years.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FNUM general secretary Mr Peter
OL,20,FHeathfield described the result as
OL,21,Fdisappointing but not unexpected.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-03-85 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
