CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A South African church leader and more
OL,6, than 200 of his supporters have been
OL,7, arrested in Cape Town as they tried to
OL,8, march on Parliament.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThey were hoping to protest at last
OL,11,Fweek's police shootings in Uitenhage in
OL,12,Fwhich 19 black people died.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FDr Alan Boesak, president of the World
OL,15,FAlliance of Reformed Churches, had
OL,16,Fearlier led a multi-racial ecumenical
OL,17,Fchurch service.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FPolice said 44 whites and two other
OL,20,Fchurch leaders were among those held.
OL,21,FThey have been charged with staging an
OL,22,Fillegal gathering and will appear in
OL,23,Fcourt tomorrow.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     GG6/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Soviet news agency TASS today
OL,6, expressed regret over the incident in
OL,7, which a US military liaison officer in
OL,8, Germany was shot by a Soviet guard.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FIt attacked the USA for spreading a
OL,11,F"deliberately false" version of
OL,12,FSunday's incident and accused the dead
OL,13,Fman, Maj Arthur Nicholson, of spying.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FUS officials have claimed that Maj
OL,16,FNicholson was left for an hour without
OL,17,Fmedical help after he was shot.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FHis body has been flown to an American
OL,20,Fbase at Frankfurt and will be taken on
OL,21,Fto America for burial.
OL,22,B
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-03-85 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49607
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,U V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0Q    GG7/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,U V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,4,F              C
OL,5, Soviet news agency TASS said that Maj
OL,6, Nicholson was taking photographs at a
OL,7, closed Soviet military installation
OL,8, near Ludwigslust when seen by a sentry.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe soviet officer demanded in Russian
OL,11,Fand German that he stop said TASS.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FWhen Maj Nicholson, not yet identified
OL,14,Fas a US soldier, did not stop and tried
OL,15,Fto escape a warning shot was fired.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FThe sentry was then "compelled to use
OL,18,Fhis weapon and the violator was killed
OL,19,Fby gunfire", TASS said.
OL,20,F
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-03-85 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49608
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,U V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0Q     G8/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,U V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,4,F              C
OL,5, Soviet news agency TASS said after the
OL,6, shooting of an intruder at a military
OL,7, installation in East Germany he was
OL,8, identified as a member of a US mission.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FTASS said Maj Nicholson and Sgt J
OL,11,FSchatz had entered the territory of the
OL,12,Finstallation despite warning signs in
OL,13,FRussian and German.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FSgt Schatz remained in their car while
OL,16,FMaj Nicholson "conducted this spying
OL,17,Foperation", said TASS.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FTASS said the US servicemen's actions
OL,20,Fwere "gross violations" of the 1947
OL,21,Fagreement under which the US mission in
OL,22,FPotsdam was established.
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 26-03-85
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     GG9/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,U V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The United States said the US army
OL,6, major was left to die after he was
OL,7, shot by a Soviet guard in East Germany.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FIt claimed Maj Arthur Nicholson was
OL,10,Fleft for an hour without medical help.
OL,11,F
OL,12,FPresident Ronald Reagan said he was
OL,13,F"shocked and saddened" by the incident
OL,14,Fand denied Maj Nicholson was a spy, as
OL,15,Fthe Soviet Union had charged.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FThe major's body has been flown to a US
OL,18,Fbase at Frankfurt and will be taken on
OL,19,Fto the United States for burial.
OL,20,F
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-03-85 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49610
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The 3,500 hourly-paid workers at the
OL,6, Yarrow shipyard on the Clyde have
OL,7, occupied the yard.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FThe action is in protest at the
OL,10,Fgovernment's agreement to the sale of
OL,11,Fthe yard by British Shipbuilders to the
OL,12,FGEC company.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FThe men claim they were not properly
OL,15,Fconsulted and say the occupation will
OL,16,Fcontinue until a new contract of
OL,17,Femployment and pay deal are negotiated.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FWork on two warships in the yard is to
OL,20,Fstop and nothing is to be allowed in or
OL,21,Fout of the yard.
OL,22,B
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-03-85 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G11/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The Yarrow sale, first big step in the
OL,6, government's plan to privatise warship
OL,7, yards, was announced yesterday.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FThe yard made #11 million profit last
OL,10,Fyear; it has orders for two type-22
OL,11,Ffrigates and the contract to build the
OL,12,Ffirst of the new type-23 frigates.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FShop stewards say British Shipbuilders
OL,15,Fbroke a pledge to give them three
OL,16,Fweeks' notice to reach agreement with a
OL,17,Fnew owner before any sale is finalised.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FYarrow workers may reckon they have
OL,20,Fbeen held back in pay terms by linking
OL,21,Fwith British Shipbuilders' loss-making
OL,22,Fmerchant yards.
OL,23,T                     D]CFrom 26-03-85
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G12/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A preliminary inquiry at a Belfast
OL,6, court into alleged protection rackets
OL,7, in the city has been stopped.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FThree men who faced charges relating to
OL,10,Frackets said to have been run on
OL,11,Fbuilding sites have been released.
OL,13,FYesterday, prosecution witnesses in the
OL,14,Fcase had been allowed to wear hoods and
OL,15,Fmasks as they feared for their lives.
OL,17,FA lawyer said the Director of Public
OL,18,FProsecutions had halted the case.
OL,20,FHe said this was in view of yesterday's
OL,21,Fproceedings and because no witness felt
OL,22,Fable to provide his name.
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 26-03-85
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49613
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G13/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A Methodist minister was jailed today
OL,6, for four years after pleading guilty to
OL,7, mutilating corpses and threatening in a
OL,8, letter to kill a child.
OL,10,FChester Crown Court heard that the
OL,11,Fmutilation was discovered when police
OL,12,Finterviewed the Rev Emyr Owen about the
OL,13,Fletter.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FHis handwriting was recognised from a
OL,16,FNew Testament which he had given as a
OL,17,Fconfirmation present.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FOwen allegedly told police he had two
OL,20,Fpersonalities, one the caring priest
OL,21,Fand another known as Emyr Ddrwg or Emyr
OL,22,Fthe Bad.
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 26-03-85
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49614
SC,0014
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774489432
OL,1,U V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0Q    G14/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,U V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,4,F              C
OL,5, Methodist minister Emyr Owen lived a
OL,6, double life.
OL,8,FWhen police searched his home, they
OL,9,Ffound a mass of pornographic literature
OL,10,F
OL,11,FOwen, 62, of Tywyn, Gwynedd, pleaded
OL,12,Fguilty to charges of mutilating corpses
OL,13,Fbetween 1976 and 1984.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FHe also admitted writing a letter in
OL,16,Fwhich he threatened to murder a girl.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FJailing Owen, Mr Justice Evans told him
OL,19,Fhis crimes had "abused the trust of the
OL,20,Fliving just as you dishonoured the
OL,21,Fdead."
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-03-85 / teletextarchive.com
